    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1219">

                <pb facs="1167" n="1155" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg1155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Turkey/340: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Matthews</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi><anchor n="54" xml:id="d1219-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-02-18T00:00:00+01:00">February 18,
                            1943—midnight.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 19—12:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1275. I took up with the Foreign Office this morning the subject matter of the
                    Department’s telegram No. 1052, February 17, 1 p.m. and was given oral
                    assurances by Sir Orme Sargent<anchor n="55" xml:id="d1219-f2"/> that
                    appropriate instructions would be sent to the British Ambassador at
                        Ankara.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d1219-f3"/> He welcomed the suggestion and
                    remarked that one of the principal problems at present with regard to chrome
                    above ground is the need of vigilance to avoid “pilfering” and to hasten
                    transport from the mines to ports.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matthews</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1219-f1" n="54" type="source" xml:id="d1219-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Ambassador in Turkey in telegram No. 157, February 22, 10
                    p.m.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1219-f2" n="55" xml:id="d1219-f2-content">
                <p>British Deputy Under Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1219-f3" n="56" xml:id="d1219-f3-content">
                <p>Sir Hughe M. Knatchbull-Hugessen.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
